-- הסכם קיבוצי מיוחד — גמול ניהול אשכולות גנים (17.6.2021): for the
-- kindergarten cluster managers of ordinary education in the State's
-- service, from 1.9.2021. It amends the reform agreement as the completion
-- agreement of 29.2.2012 (§82) left it: §144ג(א)'s cluster-management
-- allowance, 13% of the combined salary, becomes 25% in a cluster of up to
-- six kindergartens and 28% in one of seven or more; and a new §144ה lets
-- the Ministry employ a cluster manager it finds needed beyond a full
-- position — frontal hours only, within daily and weekly caps, at 100% of
-- the hour value, with pension contributions. §§133ב and 134 (the mother
-- kindergarten teacher, age hours) apply to cluster managers.
--
-- §144 as §82 of the completion agreement wrote it is encoded in that
-- agreement's module, imported: what this agreement changes is written here,
-- dated, and the rest (§144א's week, §144ג(ב)–(ד)) is the imported rules.
-- The hour value is the base agreement's §31, imported.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT conventions
IMPORT parties
IMPORT `base-agreement-31`
IMPORT `base-agreement-33`
IMPORT `2012-02-29_ofek-hadash_amendment_hascam-hashlama`

§ `הסכם קיבוצי מיוחד — גמול ניהול אשכולות גנים — 17.6.2021`

-- akn:preamble The agreement's frame: a label row with no text of its own.
-- akn:preamble/p1 The document's title; no rule.

-- The day of signing, written in by hand.
@ref akn:preamble/p2
`the signing of the cluster managers' agreement` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 17 6 2021

-- akn:preamble/p3 The registration stamp under the Collective Agreements Law (12.12.2022, no. 308/2022); no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p4 A note that the first page is initialled in its margin; no rule.

-- The parties: the State, by the Treasury's wages commissioner and the
-- Ministry of Education's director-general, and the teachers' union, by its
-- secretary-general.
@ref akn:preamble/p5 akn:preamble/p6 akn:preamble/p8 akn:preamble/p9
`the cluster managers' agreement's parties` MEANS LIST `the State`, `the teachers' union`

-- akn:preamble/p7 "On the one side"; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p10 "On the other side"; no rule.

-- The recitals name the instrument this agreement amends: the reform
-- agreements of 10.9.07 and 25.12.08 ("הסכם אופק חדש"), as the completion
-- agreement of 29.2.2012 updated them — together "הסכם רפורמת אופק". Its
-- §144 is the completion agreement's §82, the module imported above.
@ref akn:preamble/p11 akn:preamble/p12
`the reform agreement this agreement amends was completed on` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 29 2 2012

-- akn:preamble/p13 A recital: the parties negotiated the allowance's rate and employment beyond 100%; §§ד–ה below are what they agreed.
-- akn:preamble/p14 A recital: the parties anchor what they agreed in this agreement; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p15 The words of agreement that introduce the clauses; no rule.

§§ `א. כללי`

DECLARE `part of the cluster managers' agreement` IS ONE OF
    `its preamble`
    `its annexes`
    `its clauses`

-- 1: the preamble and the annexes are an inseparable part of it. (The
-- agreement attaches no annex.)
@ref akn:art_1
GIVEN p IS A `part of the cluster managers' agreement`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `binds as the cluster managers' agreement` p IF
    TRUE

#ASSERT `binds as the cluster managers' agreement` `its preamble`

-- 2: the headings are for convenience and do not bear on its reading.
@ref akn:art_2
GIVEN `the reading without the headings` IS A STRING, `the reading the headings suggest` IS A STRING
GIVETH A STRING
DECIDE `the reading the cluster managers' agreement takes` `the reading without the headings` `the reading the headings suggest` IS
    `the reading without the headings`

DECLARE `gender of a word in the cluster managers' agreement` IS ONE OF `written in the masculine`, `written in the feminine`

-- 3: the masculine or the feminine is for convenience; all of it applies to
-- women and men alike.
@ref akn:art_3
GIVEN g IS A `gender of a word in the cluster managers' agreement`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a word of the cluster managers' agreement applies to women and men alike` g IF
    TRUE

§§ `ב. תחולה`

@desc A teaching employee, as far as the cluster managers' agreement asks who it covers.
DECLARE `kindergarten cluster employee` HAS
    `ranked on the teaching employees' scale`        IS A BOOLEAN
    `in the State's service`                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `manages kindergarten clusters in ordinary education` IS A BOOLEAN
    `her share of a position as a cluster manager`    IS A NUMBER @desc the part of her position in which she manages kindergarten clusters

-- 4: every employee on the teaching employees' scale who manages
-- kindergarten clusters in ordinary education in the State's service ("a
-- kindergarten cluster manager"), for the part of her position in which she
-- does: the share the agreement reaches, 0 where it does not.
@ref akn:art_4
GIVEN e IS A `kindergarten cluster employee`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a kindergarten cluster manager in ordinary education` e IF
        e's `ranked on the teaching employees' scale`
    AND e's `in the State's service`
    AND e's `manages kindergarten clusters in ordinary education`

GIVEN e IS A `kindergarten cluster employee`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the share of her position the cluster managers' agreement reaches` e IS
    IF `a kindergarten cluster manager in ordinary education` e
    THEN e's `her share of a position as a cluster manager`
    ELSE 0

`a cluster manager who also teaches` MEANS
    `kindergarten cluster employee` WITH
        `ranked on the teaching employees' scale`        IS TRUE
        `in the State's service`                          IS TRUE
        `manages kindergarten clusters in ordinary education` IS TRUE
        `her share of a position as a cluster manager`    IS 0.8
#ASSERT `the share of her position the cluster managers' agreement reaches` `a cluster manager who also teaches` EQUALS 0.8

§§ `ג. תחילה`

-- 5: it begins on 1.9.21 ("the commencement"), a day after the period its
-- exhaustion of claims and industrial peace cover ends (§§8 and 10).
@ref akn:art_5
`the commencement of the cluster managers' agreement` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2021

§§ `ד. תיקון סעיף 144ג להסכם רפורמת אופק`

-- From the commencement §144ג(א) reads: (1) in a cluster of up to 6
-- kindergartens, 25% of the combined salary; (2) in a cluster of 7 or
-- more, 28%. Before it, the completion agreement's 13% (imported). "עד 6"
-- counts whole kindergartens and the next row opens at 7, so 6 is in the
-- first row (recorded under thresholds.until's exceptions); "7 ומעלה"
-- takes 7 in. The day is in (convention dates.start).
@ref akn:part_4__para_1
GIVEN kindergartens IS A NUMBER, d IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the cluster-management allowance rate on` kindergartens d IS
    IF d `is on or after` `the commencement of the cluster managers' agreement`
    THEN (IF kindergartens AT MOST 6 THEN 25% ELSE 28%)
    ELSE `the cluster-management allowance rate`

-- §144ג(ד), unchanged: one with a trailing allowance gets the higher of the
-- two — the completion agreement's rule, at the rate in force on the day.
GIVEN kindergartens IS A NUMBER, `combined salary` IS A NUMBER, `the trailing allowance` IS A NUMBER, d IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the cluster-management allowance on` kindergartens `combined salary` `the trailing allowance` d IS
    max (`the cluster-management allowance rate on` kindergartens d TIMES `combined salary`) `the trailing allowance`

#ASSERT `the cluster-management allowance rate on` 6 `the commencement of the cluster managers' agreement` EQUALS 25%
#ASSERT `the cluster-management allowance rate on` 7 `the commencement of the cluster managers' agreement` EQUALS 28%
#ASSERT `the cluster-management allowance on` 7 10000 0 `the commencement of the cluster managers' agreement` EQUALS 2800
-- The day before, the completion agreement's rule, whatever the cluster.
#ASSERT (    `the cluster-management allowance on` 7 10000 0 (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 8 2021)
         EQUALS `the cluster-management allowance` 10000 0)
-- A trailing allowance above the new rate still wins.
#ASSERT `the cluster-management allowance on` 4 10000 3000 `the commencement of the cluster managers' agreement` EQUALS 3000

§§ `ה. היקף העסקה — סעיף 144ה`

DECLARE `cluster manager employment action` IS ONE OF
    `decide by the published criteria that a cluster manager is needed beyond a full position`
    `employ the cluster manager beyond a full position, by §144ה's rules`

-- 6, §144ה opening: a cluster manager whom the Ministry of Education
-- decides, by criteria the teaching personnel division formulates and
-- publishes, is needed beyond a full position may be employed beyond it, by
-- the rules below — an exception to §144א(ב)'s full position only.
@ref akn:art_6
`deciding that a cluster manager is needed beyond a full position` MEANS
    PARTY `the Ministry of Education`
    MAY   `decide by the published criteria that a cluster manager is needed beyond a full position`
    HENCE (PARTY `the Ministry of Education`
           MAY   `employ the cluster manager beyond a full position, by §144ה's rules`)

@ref akn:art_6
GIVEN `found needed by the Ministry` IS A BOOLEAN, `by criteria the teaching personnel division formulated and published` IS A BOOLEAN, d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a cluster manager may be employed beyond a full position` `found needed by the Ministry` `by criteria the teaching personnel division formulated and published` d IF
        d `is on or after` `the commencement of the cluster managers' agreement`
    AND `found needed by the Ministry`
    AND `by criteria the teaching personnel division formulated and published`

-- Before §144ה, a cluster manager's position is a full one only (§144א(ב)).
#ASSERT NOT `a cluster manager may be employed beyond a full position` TRUE TRUE (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 8 2021)
#ASSERT `a kindergarten cluster manager's position` EQUALS 1

-- (א) the hours beyond a full position are frontal teaching hours only; (ב)
-- frontal, individual and stay hours together come to 8.5 a day, Sunday to
-- Thursday, 5 on Friday, and 42 a week, at most. The caps are §33(ד)(2)'s
-- for a teacher; they are written here as §144ה states them.
DECLARE `kind of hour beyond a full position` IS ONE OF
    `a frontal teaching hour`
    `an individual hour`
    `a stay hour`
    `a management hour`

@ref akn:art_6
GIVEN h IS A `kind of hour beyond a full position`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an hour a cluster manager may work beyond a full position` h IF
    h EQUALS `a frontal teaching hour`

@ref akn:art_6
GIVEN `hours each day, Sunday to Friday` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a cluster manager's week beyond a full position keeps the caps` `hours each day, Sunday to Friday` IF
        all (GIVEN h YIELD h AT MOST 8.5) (take 5 `hours each day, Sunday to Friday`)
    AND all (GIVEN h YIELD h AT MOST 5) (drop 5 `hours each day, Sunday to Friday`)
    AND sum `hours each day, Sunday to Friday` AT MOST 42

#ASSERT NOT `an hour a cluster manager may work beyond a full position` `a management hour`
#ASSERT `a cluster manager's week beyond a full position keeps the caps` (LIST 8.5, 8.5, 8.5, 8.5, 8, 0)
#ASSERT NOT `a cluster manager's week beyond a full position keeps the caps` (LIST 8.5, 8.5, 8.5, 8.5, 8.5, 0)
-- The same caps as §33(ד)(2)'s, on the same weeks.
#ASSERT (    `a cluster manager's week beyond a full position keeps the caps` (LIST 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 2)
         EQUALS `the week beyond 100% keeps the caps` (LIST 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 2))

-- (ג) an hour beyond a full position is paid at 100% of the hour value, its
-- base §31(א)(1)'s and its computation §31(ב)'s (imported).
@ref akn:art_6
GIVEN p IS A `pay for the hour value`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `pay for a cluster manager's hour beyond a full position` p IS
    100% TIMES `the hour value` (`the base under 31(א)(1)` p)

`a cluster manager for the hour value` MEANS
    `pay for the hour value` WITH
        `combined salary`             IS 7794
        `special-education allowance` IS 0
        `pensionable role allowances` IS 779.4
        `a special-education teacher substituting in a special-education class` IS FALSE
#ASSERT `pay for a cluster manager's hour beyond a full position` `a cluster manager for the hour value` EQUALS 50

-- (ד) on that pay, contributions to a pension provident fund: the employer
-- 13⅓% (8⅓% severance and 5% benefits), the employee 5%, by the rules of
-- the agreement of 27.12.84 ("הסכם דפנה"), which is not in the corpus.
-- F-ofek-hadash-gan-cluster-2021-a: (ד) speaks of "the pay in paragraph (3)
-- above"; §144ה's paragraphs are lettered (א)–(ד), and the pay is (ג)'s.
-- (ד) is read as speaking of (ג)'s pay (convention reading.misprint).
@ref akn:art_6
`the employer's severance contribution on a cluster manager's hours beyond a full position` MEANS 25/3 DIVIDED BY 100
`the employer's benefits contribution on a cluster manager's hours beyond a full position` MEANS 5%
`the employee's contribution on a cluster manager's hours beyond a full position` MEANS 5%

#ASSERT (    `the employer's severance contribution on a cluster manager's hours beyond a full position`
           PLUS `the employer's benefits contribution on a cluster manager's hours beyond a full position`
         EQUALS 40/3 DIVIDED BY 100)

`the paragraphs of §144ה` MEANS LIST "(א)", "(ב)", "(ג)", "(ד)"
`§144ה(ד) cites a paragraph (3) that §144ה does not have` MEANS
    NOT elem "(3)" `the paragraphs of §144ה`
#ASSERT `§144ה(ד) cites a paragraph (3) that §144ה does not have`

§§ `ו. שעות גיל ומשרת אם`

-- 7: for the avoidance of doubt, §133ב (the mother kindergarten teacher) and
-- §134 (age hours) apply to cluster managers — as the completion agreement
-- (§75) worded them, imported.
@ref akn:art_7
GIVEN `her position` IS A NUMBER, `took no absence all year` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `a mother cluster manager's position for the year` `her position` `took no absence all year` IS
    `a mother kindergarten teacher's position for the year` `her position` `took no absence all year`

@ref akn:art_7
GIVEN `an existing kindergarten teacher` IS A BOOLEAN, `age on 31 December of the school year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `a cluster manager's age-hours reduction` `an existing kindergarten teacher` `age on 31 December of the school year` IS
    `a kindergarten teacher's age-hours reduction` `an existing kindergarten teacher` `age on 31 December of the school year`

#ASSERT `a mother cluster manager's position for the year` 1 TRUE EQUALS 1.1
#ASSERT `a cluster manager's age-hours reduction` TRUE 56 EQUALS 4

§§ `ז. מיצוי תביעות`

`the end of the period the cluster managers' agreement settles` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 31 8 2021

DECLARE `cluster managers' claim action` IS ONE OF
    `raise a claim on a matter the cluster managers' agreement settles, for the period to 31.8.2021`
    `strike or lock out over a matter the cluster managers' agreement settles, for the period to 31.8.2021`

-- 8: it fully exhausts the parties' claims on the matters it settles, for
-- the period to 31.8.2021; 9: the exhaustion provisions that bind the
-- parties, or will, stand.
-- F-ofek-hadash-gan-cluster-2021-b: the period the exhaustion (8) and the
-- industrial peace (10) cover ends on 31.8.2021, the day before the
-- agreement begins (5): neither reaches a day of its own term. They are
-- read as printed (convention reading.as-printed).
@ref akn:art_8 akn:art_9
`no further claims on what the cluster managers' agreement settles` MEANS
    PARTY `the teachers' union`
    SHANT `raise a claim on a matter the cluster managers' agreement settles, for the period to 31.8.2021`

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the cluster managers' agreement's exhaustion covers` d IF
    d `is on or before` `the end of the period the cluster managers' agreement settles`

`the exhaustion and the peace end before the cluster managers' agreement begins` MEANS
        NOT `the cluster managers' agreement's exhaustion covers` `the commencement of the cluster managers' agreement`
    AND `the end of the period the cluster managers' agreement settles` `is on or before` `the commencement of the cluster managers' agreement`
#ASSERT `the exhaustion and the peace end before the cluster managers' agreement begins`

§§ `ח. שקט תעשייתי`

-- 10: neither party, nor its members or units, takes a strike or lockout,
-- whole or partial, or any other organised harm to the work, against the
-- other on the matters the agreement settles, for the period to 31.8.2021;
-- 11: the industrial-peace provisions that bind the parties stand.
@ref akn:art_10 akn:art_11
`industrial peace under the cluster managers' agreement` MEANS
    (PARTY `the State`
     SHANT `strike or lock out over a matter the cluster managers' agreement settles, for the period to 31.8.2021`)
    RAND
    (PARTY `the teachers' union`
     SHANT `strike or lock out over a matter the cluster managers' agreement settles, for the period to 31.8.2021`)

-- akn:conclusions The sign-off: a label row with no text of its own.
-- akn:conclusions/p1 "In witness whereof"; no rule.
-- akn:conclusions/p2 The signatures; no rule.
-- akn:conclusions/t1 The parties' signature headings; no rule.
